cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CSBQ, please cite both the software and the paper below."
type: software
title: "CSBQ: Convergent slender-body quadrature"
authors:
  - given-names: Dhairya
    family-names: Malhotra
  - given-names: Alex
    family-names: Barnett
abstract: "A high-performance parallel C++ implementation of a high-order adaptive Nyström quadrature for the boundary integral equations arising in 3D Laplace and Stokes Dirichlet and rigid mobility boundary-value problems for closed loop filaments of arbitrarily small circular cross-section. Also MATLAB codes for the classical slender-body theory approximation."
repository-code: "https://github.com/dmalhotra/CSBQ"
url: "https://csbq.readthedocs.io"
identifiers:
